[xUnit.net 00:02:35.19]       OPEN RULING — Meals owner. A shared mailbox can claim another employee's invitation because the confirmed-email match does not require the address to identify ONE account (Identity's RequireUniqueEmail is unset and AspNetUsers.Email carries no unique index). Four remedies are written up — enforce address uniqueness, bind the invitation to an account id at issue, refuse an address resolving to more than one account, or require a second channel — and choosing between them changes what a company admin must type, so it is not a test's call. This fact states the property every remedy must satisfy and is unskipped the day one lands; A_shared_mailbox_colleague_can_still_take_the_membership_the_company_meant_for_someone_else fails on that same day and is what makes this skip impossible to forget.
